{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 32, :comments ["<b>A sabbath of solemn rest it is.</b> The word is written with a vav and is read as written, as I explained in the perasha of Aḥarei Mot." "<b>And you shall afflict your souls on the ninth of the month.</b> Our Rabbis interpreted: is it on the ninth of the month that we fast, etc.? And one does not interpret thus regarding matzot, even though it is written concerning them ״בערב תאכלו מצות״, because here ענוי is written, regarding the ninth it is written." "<b>On the ninth of the month, at evening.</b> Its cantillation proves that it does not refer back to ועניתם, but rather to teach: its evening — until the evening of the tenth." "<b>From evening to evening you shall rest.</b> From here that the night follows from the coming day." "<b>You shall rest.</b> Every rest that you observe — whether Shabbat, whether Yom HaKippurim, whether a festival — you must add to it, whether before it or after it." "<b>Your Sabbath.</b> This is Yom HaKippurim, which was given to Israel for rest and for a sacred convocation. But the seventh day is not called a Sabbath for Israel, but rather a Sabbath for HaShem, on account of 'for on it He rested.'"], :book :leviticus, :voice :chizkuni, :lang :en, :chapter 23, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T15:14:51.291672159Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}